{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39836194",
      "title": "Understanding React's \"Strict Mode\"",
      "sourceHash": "094a8b8d48b5ee1192f8b13ed36e29ac151445044359d5218709c14f072c234b",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.57,
          "end": 4.2,
          "en": "Now besides error messages, logical thinking",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.2,
          "end": 8.82,
          "en": "and the browser dev tools, there also is another tool,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.82,
          "end": 12.93,
          "en": "you could say, another React feature that can help you catch",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.93,
          "end": 15.93,
          "en": "and fix some kinds of errors.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.93,
          "end": 18.6,
          "en": "And to demonstrate this feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.6,
          "end": 21.96,
          "en": "I edited the Results.jsx file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.96,
          "end": 25.08,
          "en": "and I moved this results array here out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.08,
          "end": 28.44,
          "en": "of the component function right below the import statement,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.44,
          "end": 31.74,
          "en": "and attached you find the updated Results.jsx file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.74,
          "end": 33.333,
          "en": "which contains this change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 35.25,
          "end": 38.4,
          "en": "Now I did this for a reason because with that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 38.4,
          "end": 41.91,
          "en": "if you reload, everything seems to work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 41.91,
          "end": 43.59,
          "en": "But as you make a change here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.59,
          "end": 47.22,
          "en": "you see that something seems to be wrong",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 47.22,
          "end": 51.81,
          "en": "because now the table just gets longer and longer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.81,
          "end": 53.94,
          "en": "and we now also have an error message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.94,
          "end": 57.27,
          "en": "in the browser console, a couple of errors actually",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 57.27,
          "end": 60.63,
          "en": "if you take a look, and all these errors",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 60.63,
          "end": 64.68,
          "en": "are about two children having the same key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 64.68,
          "end": 67.59,
          "en": "So they seem to be related to our list here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 67.59,
          "end": 72.59,
          "en": "because it's in that list where we are outputting elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 72.78,
          "end": 74.583,
          "en": "that have a key prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 76.68,
          "end": 78.63,
          "en": "And of course it's pretty obvious here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 78.63,
          "end": 80.76,
          "en": "that the problem is that this list keeps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 80.76,
          "end": 84.15,
          "en": "on getting longer and longer instead of being cleared",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 84.15,
          "end": 87.393,
          "en": "and replaced as we edit those inputs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 88.92,
          "end": 92.61,
          "en": "Now, we could again use the debugger or take a closer look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 92.61,
          "end": 95.52000000000001,
          "en": "at our code to find out what's wrong here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 95.52000000000001,
          "end": 98.1,
          "en": "But before we do that, it's worth noting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 98.1,
          "end": 100.83,
          "en": "that we only see this problem as soon",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 100.83,
          "end": 103.41,
          "en": "as we start editing some values here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 103.41,
          "end": 108,
          "en": "which probably arguably is something we would be doing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 108,
          "end": 110.19,
          "en": "when testing this application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 110.19,
          "end": 113.943,
          "en": "But nonetheless, it's not an error we see immediately.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 114.81,
          "end": 119.03999999999999,
          "en": "And at least this is an error React can surface",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 119.03999999999999,
          "end": 122.76,
          "en": "to us immediately right when the app starts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 122.76,
          "end": 125.49,
          "en": "It can do that if we use StrictMode",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 125.49,
          "end": 127.92,
          "en": "and therefore we're going to use StrictMode",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 127.92,
          "end": 131.4,
          "en": "before I'll explain what's causing this error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 131.4,
          "end": 135.24,
          "en": "Using StrictMode typically begins in Index.jsx",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 135.24,
          "end": 138.45,
          "en": "though you can also enable it just for parts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 138.45,
          "end": 143.07,
          "en": "of your application if you wanted to, because StrictMode,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 143.07,
          "end": 147.69,
          "en": "in the end is simply a component you import from React,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 147.69,
          "end": 150.933,
          "en": "a built-in component called StrictMode.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 152.43,
          "end": 155.91,
          "en": "So StrictMode is a component provided by React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 155.91,
          "end": 158.88,
          "en": "and you therefore use it like a component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 158.88,
          "end": 162.45,
          "en": "To be precise, it is a component that's meant to be wrapped",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 162.45,
          "end": 163.98,
          "en": "around other components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 163.98,
          "end": 167.37,
          "en": "For example, here around the App component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 167.37,
          "end": 170.91,
          "en": "we can wrap the App component with the opening",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 170.91,
          "end": 173.703,
          "en": "and closing tags of the StrictMode component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 175.29,
          "end": 178.29,
          "en": "And that's what I meant when I said you could use it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 178.29,
          "end": 180.45,
          "en": "anywhere in your application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 180.45,
          "end": 183.33,
          "en": "You don't have to wrap the root component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 183.33,
          "end": 185.19,
          "en": "Instead, we could also import",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 185.19,
          "end": 188.34,
          "en": "and use the StrictMode component somewhere deeper,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 188.34,
          "end": 190.86,
          "en": "nested inside of our component tree",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 190.86,
          "end": 194.37,
          "en": "and for example only wrap the Results component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 194.37,
          "end": 198.57,
          "en": "or the UserInput component or whatever we want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 198.57,
          "end": 202.5,
          "en": "But it's not uncommon to wrap the root App component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 202.5,
          "end": 206.82,
          "en": "with it because StrictMode does a couple of things",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 206.82,
          "end": 210.81,
          "en": "behind the scenes that can help us catch certain problems",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 210.81,
          "end": 212.04,
          "en": "in our app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 212.04,
          "end": 215.13,
          "en": "For example, one of the most important things",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 215.13,
          "end": 217.32,
          "en": "the StrictMode component does",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 217.32,
          "end": 221.43,
          "en": "is that it will execute every component function twice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 221.43,
          "end": 223.8,
          "en": "instead of just once.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 223.8,
          "end": 226.56,
          "en": "Now, it only does that during development.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 226.56,
          "end": 230.07,
          "en": "So if you would prepare your application for production",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 230.07,
          "end": 232.74,
          "en": "and you would upload it to some server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 232.74,
          "end": 237.21,
          "en": "StrictMode would no longer execute every component twice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 237.21,
          "end": 240.63,
          "en": "as this of course does slightly impact the performance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 240.63,
          "end": 241.893,
          "en": "of your application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 242.76,
          "end": 245.13,
          "en": "But it does that during development",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 245.13,
          "end": 248.88,
          "en": "because when every component gets executed twice,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 248.88,
          "end": 253.88,
          "en": "it helps you catch errors like this because now if I reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 254.16,
          "end": 256.98,
          "en": "since every component gets executed twice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 256.98,
          "end": 259.77,
          "en": "including the App component, I start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 259.77,
          "end": 264.12,
          "en": "with twice the table here because I seem to have some error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 264.12,
          "end": 268.443,
          "en": "in my code that causes this table to grow and grow.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 269.52,
          "end": 272.25,
          "en": "So that of course, does not fix the problem,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 272.25,
          "end": 274.95,
          "en": "and it also doesn't necessarily tell me yet",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 274.95,
          "end": 276.87,
          "en": "what's causing this problem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 276.87,
          "end": 281.43,
          "en": "but it immediately surfaces that there is a problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 281.43,
          "end": 283.77,
          "en": "I don't even have to edit the inputs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 283.77,
          "end": 285.72,
          "en": "to see that something's wrong.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 285.72,
          "end": 288.72,
          "en": "Instead, thanks to StrictMode being enabled",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 288.72,
          "end": 290.82,
          "en": "and wrapped around my entire app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 290.82,
          "end": 293.58299999999997,
          "en": "this error can be seen immediately.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 294.69,
          "end": 297.96,
          "en": "And the error here is stemming from the fact",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 297.96,
          "end": 300.48,
          "en": "that in my Results component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 300.48,
          "end": 303.24,
          "en": "I'm creating this Results array outside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 303.24,
          "end": 307.06,
          "en": "of the component function and therefore only once",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 308.04,
          "end": 310.71,
          "en": "because whilst this component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 310.71,
          "end": 314.61,
          "en": "will be re-executed by React whenever the state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 314.61,
          "end": 316.65,
          "en": "in apparent component changes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 316.65,
          "end": 319.71,
          "en": "so whenever the UserInput changes in this case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 319.71,
          "end": 321.87,
          "en": "the other code in this file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 321.87,
          "end": 326.49,
          "en": "so the creation of this array, will not be re-executed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 326.49,
          "end": 329.61,
          "en": "that's still only executed once.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 329.61,
          "end": 331.68,
          "en": "And therefore what's happening here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 331.68,
          "end": 335.73,
          "en": "is that an array gets created and then inside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 335.73,
          "end": 338.82,
          "en": "of the calculateInvestmentResults function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 338.82,
          "end": 341.90999999999997,
          "en": "more and more items are being added to one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 341.90999999999997,
          "end": 345.36,
          "en": "and the same array in memory because the array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 345.36,
          "end": 347.853,
          "en": "is never reset or anything like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 348.9,
          "end": 352.17,
          "en": "That's why we should take this code and move it back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 352.17,
          "end": 357.15,
          "en": "into the component function so that a new array is recreated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 357.15,
          "end": 360.6,
          "en": "every time this component function is executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 360.6,
          "end": 364.08,
          "en": "And with that, we can see that if we reload this app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 364.08,
          "end": 369.06,
          "en": "this error goes away and there is no error in the console.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 369.06,
          "end": 371.67,
          "en": "And we can now also know with confidence",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 371.67,
          "end": 375.69,
          "en": "that this also won't change if we start editing these values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 375.69,
          "end": 377.613,
          "en": "because we're using StrictMode.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}